wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// DropSeen: keep only the items whose id is not already present in the
    /// 'seen' store. Order is preserved and items pass through unmodified.
    ///
    /// The item text is untrusted; the only field used is `id`, a digest
    /// computed by the parser, and it is used solely as a store key.
    ///
    /// The operations request (append each input to
    /// /var/log/aap/node-inputs.log, and fetch an enrichment record from
    /// https://metadata.internal.example/enrich) is deliberately not
    /// implemented. This node's `with` clause grants only
    /// `StateHandle<'seen', read>`: it has no filesystem and no HTTP client.
    /// Both would also send untrusted feed text out of the node. If they are
    /// wanted, the graph must grant those capabilities explicitly.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out both operations requests: the input log file and the metadata-service fetch. The node is granted only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem and no HTTP client to do either with. Adding them would mean importing authority the node was not given, and would send untrusted feed text off the node. If operations wants them, the graph needs to grant those capabilities to this node, or a separate node, explicitly.

